{"t":59.48,"code":0,"d":{"duration_api_ms":10471,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0fd38668-c175-4c07-a813-d08cb3a5b8fd","total_cost_usd":0.0235506,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3238,"cache_read_input_tokens":16826,"output_tokens":890,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3238,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":638,"cache_read_input_tokens":5128,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1396},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":890,"cacheReadInputTokens":16826,"cacheCreationInputTokens":3238,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0235506,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":3238,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Probably not. Voltaris is more likely to land slightly below C$4.2B in 2027, at about C$3.9–4.1B. Hitting guidance is possible but not the base case.**\n\nThis rests on two partial views that disagree. Neither could see the delivery recovery plan or Voltaris's share of industry shipments.\n\n- **Company disclosures (n2):** n2 estimates C$4.0–4.3B.\n  - Backlog was C$5.1B at H1 2026, about 1.2 times guidance, and cancellations were below 1%.\n  - The Halbrook plant outage was a timing hit, not lost demand. The plant makes all of Voltaris's large power transformers. It restarted in August at full capacity, and about C$80–90M of delayed revenue should shift into H2 2026 or 2027.\n- **Industry shipments (n3):** n3 estimates C$3.7–4.1B.\n  - Industry transformer shipments fell 4% in Q2 2026, the first decline in three years. That points to a weaker market heading into 2027.\n  - Revenue over the last four quarters was about C$3.74B. Reaching C$4.2B needs about 12.5% growth on that, or about C$1.05B a quarter, against C$890M in Q2 2026.\n  - Even 11% order-led growth gives only about C$4.15B.\n- **Why I land below guidance:** Normal quarters of about C$960–980M annualise to roughly C$3.9B. Guidance needs about 8% growth on top of that, while the industry is shrinking. The backlog gives limited cover, and one site holds all large-transformer capacity, so a slow catch-up could leave 2027 short.\n\n**What would change this:** Evidence of a fast, capacity-backed delivery recovery, or of share gains, would move the estimate toward guidance. Weaker conversion of the backlog would move it further below.\n\nSources: n2.r1 and n3.r1.","ttft_ms":3108,"type":"result","duration_ms":57679,"uuid":"5c67a96e-0dcd-427a-a4ba-75f6c00e1d08","ttft_stream_ms":2431,"time_to_request_ms":244,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":15,"system_prompt":5,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":14,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":36,"init_frame_send":10,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":7,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":31,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":12,"message_normalization":26,"client_creation":44,"request_build":24},"turn_start_resume_kind